  "narrative": "The new broad screens and median-complexity interaction tests are interpreted with estimates already signed to each registered direction. The main scientific finding is that two positive-direction claims were contradicted by very large opposite associations: SMARCA4 loss (H23, R28: signed +1 estimate -0.804, 95% interval -0.867 to -0.742) and PTEN loss (H39, R33: signed +1 estimate -0.239, interval -0.332 to -0.145). Because negative values of dependency_composite mean stronger dependency, these raw results are more consistent with SMARCA4-loss and PTEN-loss cells having stronger dependency scores than non-loss cells. I therefore reject H23 and H39 as positive main-effect claims, but keep both investigations active and register reversed claims because the opposite effects are substantial for SMARCA4 and above threshold for PTEN. The remaining screens are largely null: STK11 loss (H22, R27 -0.035, interval -0.111 to 0.040), ARID1A loss (H24, R29 0.052, interval -0.017 to 0.121), MTAP loss (H25, R30 0.005), PIK3CA mutation (H38, R32 0.031), and RB1 loss (H40, R34 0.091, interval -0.006 to 0.188). CDKN2A loss (H26, R31 -0.139, interval -0.213 to -0.065) is statistically nonzero and in the opposite direction, but its point estimate is below the 0.15-unit scientific threshold, so I close the positive claim without following the subthreshold opposite signal. The median-ploidy and median-mutation-burden robustness interactions for the dominant KEAP1 and TP53 effects are not supported: H58/R35 is near zero, H62/R37 and H63/R38 are near zero, and H59/R36 has point 0.119 with interval -0.005 to 0.243, which is below threshold and imprecise. I close these positive interaction claims to allocate effort toward the new reversed SMARCA4 and PTEN lines. Multiple testing is a concern for the broad screens, but the SMARCA4 interval is so far from threshold and zero that it remains compelling even with multiplicity; PTEN is also robust but smaller, so I request independent validation for H23 as the most informative comparison. Future SMARCA4 and PTEN conditional claims will test whether these associations remain after stratifying by TP53 and, for SMARCA4, KEAP1, because co-occurring genomic losses could contribute to the marginal associations. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable effects.",
  "research_notes": "Current central accepted dataset associations: H6 KEAP1 loss -> higher dependency_composite (weaker dependency) and H13 TP53 loss -> higher dependency_composite, both independently validated. New discovery evidence: H23 positive SMARCA4-loss claim is rejected, but R28 shows a very large opposite effect (raw signed -1 equivalent about +0.804 lower composite score in SMARCA4-loss cells; more negative means stronger dependency). H39 positive PTEN-loss claim is rejected, but R33 shows an opposite effect about 0.239 units below threshold direction, interval entirely beyond zero. Reversed SMARCA4 and PTEN claims are registered and should be prioritized once H23 validation is evaluated. Conditional SMARCA4 within TP53-loss/nonloss and KEAP1-loss/nonloss are registered to check co-occurrence/confounding; conditional PTEN within TP53 strata registered. Null/closed in this batch: STK11 main effect, ARID1A loss, MTAP loss, CDKN2A loss, PIK3CA mutation, RB1 loss, median-ploidy KEAP1/TP53 interactions (H58 near null; H59 point 0.119 below threshold), and median-mutation-burden KEAP1/TP53 interactions (H62, H63 near null). Previous accepted conditional robustness claims remain H14-H17 and H35. Remaining unresolved low-priority: H11 KEAP1-by-KRAS and reversed H31/H41 Cas9 attenuation. Validation requested for H23 because SMARCA4 opposite effect is the largest new signal and needs independent stability; PTEN validation may be useful later if capacity remains.",
